== 45A.1  a projection by hand (s = 3, k = 3)
entry size sqrt(s/k) = 1.0   non-zeros per row: [3, 3, 3]
d = [2.0, 0.0, 2.0, -2.0, 0.0, 2.0]  |d|^2 = 16.0  squares: [4.0, 0.0, 4.0, 4.0, 0.0, 4.0]
rows of R times d: [0.0, 0.0, -2.0]  Rd = [ 0.  0. -2.]  |Rd|^2 = 4.0
q = 0.25
sum d^4 / |d|^4 = 0.2500;  Var q = (2 + (s-3) * that)/k = 0.6667, sd 0.8165;  Gaussian sd sqrt(2/k) = 0.8165
z-score of q = 0.25: -0.919;  P(chi2_3/3 <= 0.25) = 0.1386;  P(q <= 0.25 or q >= 1.75) = 0.2930
simulation of 200000 matrices of Eq. 45.3-4: mean q 0.999  sd 0.815  share with q <= 0.25: 0.215
if the entries were N(0, 1/3) instead: sd of q would be 0.816 (same, since s = 3)
slip: forgetting the scale, i.e. using entries +-1/sqrt(k) = 0.577 gives |Rd|^2 = 1.333 and q = 0.083

